I realize {malba}, {zanba} and {pacna} are all problematical and have been 
hotly disputed.   Expectation is a key component of being optimistic or 
pessimistic, but I don't want to use {kanpe} as it is experimental.. I guess 
I was hiding behind the 'any lujvo can mean anything' screen! 

In place of {pacna} then I would propose {jijnu}.  
I prefer {jijnu} to {cinmo} as {jijnu} implies one coming to some sort of conclusion 
whereas {cinmo} may be the emotional result of such a conclusion.

> > 1) xagjijnu (optimistic)

  
j1 jijni lodu'u lonu x1 xamgu x2 x3 ku'o fasnu kei j3
 
j1 xagjijnu j3
 
> >
> > 2) xlajijnu (pessimistic)

  
j1 jijni lodu'u lonu x1 xlali x2 x3 ku'o fasnu kei j3
 
j1 xlajijnu j3

 
> > 3) xlamukpa'a (cynical)
> >
> > p1 is cynical about the motives of m3 with regard to action/event m2
> >
> 
>   Same comment as above.  I'd think cynical would be more xlamu'ixu'a,
> or xlamu'ijijnu or xlamukcni an assertion/intuition/feeling that
> someone has a "bad" motive, not a hope that they do.



So how about:
{j1 jijnu lodu'u m3 termu'i m2 lo xlali kei j3}
{j1 xlamu'ijijnu m3 m2=j3}.

totus




